{
    "chapter_num": 25,
    "verses_count": 34,
    "paragraphs_list": [
        {
            "type": "section_header",
            "text": "Abraham and Keturah"
        },
        {
            "type": "section_paragraph",
            "verses_list": [
                {
                    "num_int": 1,
                    "num_str": "1",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "Abraham again took a wife, and her name "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "ITALIC",
                            "text": "was"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " Keturah. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 2,
                    "num_str": "2",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "And she bore him Zimran, Jokshan, Medan, Midian, Ishbak, and Shuah. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 3,
                    "num_str": "3",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "Jokshan begot Sheba and Dedan. And the sons of Dedan were Asshurim, Letushim, and Leummim. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 4,
                    "num_str": "4",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "And the sons of Midian "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "ITALIC",
                            "text": "were"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " Ephah, Epher, Hanoch, Abidah, and Eldaah. All these "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "ITALIC",
                            "text": "were"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " the children of Keturah."
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "section_paragraph",
            "verses_list": [
                {
                    "num_int": 5,
                    "num_str": "5",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "And Abraham gave all that he had to Isaac. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 6,
                    "num_str": "6",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "But Abraham gave gifts to the sons of the concubines which Abraham had; and while he was still living he sent them eastward, away from Isaac his son, to the country of the east."
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "section_header",
            "text": "Abraham’s Death and Burial"
        },
        {
            "type": "section_paragraph",
            "verses_list": [
                {
                    "num_int": 7,
                    "num_str": "7",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "This "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "ITALIC",
                            "text": "is"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " the sum of the years of Abraham’s life which he lived: one hundred and seventy-five years. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 8,
                    "num_str": "8",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "Then Abraham breathed his last and died in a good old age, an old man and full "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "ITALIC",
                            "text": "of years,"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " and was gathered to his people. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 9,
                    "num_str": "9",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "And his sons Isaac and Ishmael buried him in the cave of Machpelah, which "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "ITALIC",
                            "text": "is"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " before Mamre, in the field of Ephron the son of Zohar the Hittite, "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 10,
                    "num_str": "10",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "the field which Abraham purchased from the sons of Heth. There Abraham was buried, and Sarah his wife. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 11,
                    "num_str": "11",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "And it came to pass, after the death of Abraham, that God blessed his son Isaac. And Isaac dwelt at Beer Lahai Roi."
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "section_header",
            "text": "The Families of Ishmael and Isaac"
        },
        {
            "type": "section_paragraph",
            "verses_list": [
                {
                    "num_int": 12,
                    "num_str": "12",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "Now this "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "ITALIC",
                            "text": "is"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " the genealogy of Ishmael, Abraham’s son, whom Hagar the Egyptian, Sarah’s maidservant, bore to Abraham. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 13,
                    "num_str": "13",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "And these "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "ITALIC",
                            "text": "were"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " the names of the sons of Ishmael, by their names, according to their generations: The firstborn of Ishmael, Nebajoth; then Kedar, Adbeel, Mibsam, "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 14,
                    "num_str": "14",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "Mishma, Dumah, Massa, "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 15,
                    "num_str": "15",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "FOOTNOTE",
                            "text": "MT Hadad"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "Hadar, Tema, Jetur, Naphish, and Kedemah. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 16,
                    "num_str": "16",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "These "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "ITALIC",
                            "text": "were"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " the sons of Ishmael and these "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "ITALIC",
                            "text": "were"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " their names, by their towns and their "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "FOOTNOTE",
                            "text": "camps"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "settlements, twelve princes according to their nations. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 17,
                    "num_str": "17",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "These "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "ITALIC",
                            "text": "were"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " the years of the life of Ishmael: one hundred and thirty-seven years; and he breathed his last and died, and was gathered to his people. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 18,
                    "num_str": "18",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "(They dwelt from Havilah as far as Shur, which "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "ITALIC",
                            "text": "is"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " east of Egypt as you go toward Assyria.) He "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "FOOTNOTE",
                            "text": "fell"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "died in the presence of all his brethren."
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "section_paragraph",
            "verses_list": [
                {
                    "num_int": 19,
                    "num_str": "19",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "This "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "ITALIC",
                            "text": "is"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " the genealogy of Isaac, Abraham’s son. Abraham begot Isaac. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 20,
                    "num_str": "20",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "Isaac was forty years old when he took Rebekah as wife, the daughter of Bethuel the Syrian of Padan Aram, the sister of Laban the Syrian. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 21,
                    "num_str": "21",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "Now Isaac pleaded with the "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "DIVINE_NAME",
                            "text": "Lord"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " for his wife, because she "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "ITALIC",
                            "text": "was"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " barren; and the "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "DIVINE_NAME",
                            "text": "Lord"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " granted his plea, and Rebekah his wife conceived. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 22,
                    "num_str": "22",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "But the children struggled together within her; and she said, “If "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "ITALIC",
                            "text": "all is"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " well, why "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "ITALIC",
                            "text": "am I like"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " this?” So she went to inquire of the "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "DIVINE_NAME",
                            "text": "Lord"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "."
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "section_paragraph",
            "verses_list": [
                {
                    "num_int": 23,
                    "num_str": "23",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "And the "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "DIVINE_NAME",
                            "text": "Lord"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " said to her:"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "LINE_BREAK",
                            "text": "\n"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "“Two nations "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "ITALIC",
                            "text": "are"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " in your womb,"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "LINE_BREAK",
                            "text": "\n"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "Two peoples shall be separated from your body;"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "LINE_BREAK",
                            "text": "\n"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "ITALIC",
                            "text": "One"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " people shall be stronger than the other,"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "LINE_BREAK",
                            "text": "\n"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "And the older shall serve the younger.”"
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "section_paragraph",
            "verses_list": [
                {
                    "num_int": 24,
                    "num_str": "24",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "So when her days were fulfilled "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "ITALIC",
                            "text": "for her"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " to give birth, indeed "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "ITALIC",
                            "text": "there were"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " twins in her womb. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 25,
                    "num_str": "25",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "And the first came out red. "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "ITALIC",
                            "text": "He was"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " like a hairy garment all over; so they called his name "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "FOOTNOTE",
                            "text": "Lit. Hairy"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "Esau. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 26,
                    "num_str": "26",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "Afterward his brother came out, and his hand took hold of Esau’s heel; so his name was called "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "FOOTNOTE",
                            "text": "Supplanter or Deceitful, lit. One Who Takes the Heel"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "Jacob. Isaac "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "ITALIC",
                            "text": "was"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " sixty years old when she bore them."
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "section_paragraph",
            "verses_list": [
                {
                    "num_int": 27,
                    "num_str": "27",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "So the boys grew. And Esau was a skillful hunter, a man of the field; but Jacob was a "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "FOOTNOTE",
                            "text": "Lit. complete"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "mild man, dwelling in tents. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 28,
                    "num_str": "28",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "And Isaac loved Esau because he ate "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "ITALIC",
                            "text": "of his"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " game, but Rebekah loved Jacob."
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "section_header",
            "text": "Esau Sells His Birthright"
        },
        {
            "type": "section_paragraph",
            "verses_list": [
                {
                    "num_int": 29,
                    "num_str": "29",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "Now Jacob cooked a stew; and Esau came in from the field, and he "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "ITALIC",
                            "text": "was"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " weary. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 30,
                    "num_str": "30",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "And Esau said to Jacob, “Please feed me with that same red "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "ITALIC",
                            "text": "stew,"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " for I "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "ITALIC",
                            "text": "am"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " weary.” Therefore his name was called "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "FOOTNOTE",
                            "text": "Lit. Red"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "Edom."
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "section_paragraph",
            "verses_list": [
                {
                    "num_int": 31,
                    "num_str": "31",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "But Jacob said, “Sell me your birthright as of this day.”"
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "section_paragraph",
            "verses_list": [
                {
                    "num_int": 32,
                    "num_str": "32",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "And Esau said, “Look, I "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "ITALIC",
                            "text": "am"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " about to die; so what "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "ITALIC",
                            "text": "is"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " this birthright to me?”"
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "section_paragraph",
            "verses_list": [
                {
                    "num_int": 33,
                    "num_str": "33",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "Then Jacob said, "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "FOOTNOTE",
                            "text": "Take an oath"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "“Swear to me as of this day.”"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "LINE_BREAK",
                            "text": "\n"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "So he swore to him, and sold his birthright to Jacob. "
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "section_paragraph",
            "verses_list": [
                {
                    "num_int": 34,
                    "num_str": "34",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "And Jacob gave Esau bread and stew of lentils; then he ate and drank, arose, and went his way. Thus Esau despised "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "ITALIC",
                            "text": "his"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " birthright."
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ]
        }
    ]
}